/T (Separates UI, logic and hardware so each can change independently Lets the same framework run on different SoCs, amplifiers and vehicles Isolates faults; a projection failure should not stop navigation or media Single place to enforce priority and avoid overlapping audio Well-defined, versionable, permission-checked inter-process interfaces Typed properties give apps safe, uniform access to vehicle data)
/E (Separates UI, logic and hardware so each can change independently Lets the same framework run on different SoCs, amplifiers and vehicles Isolates faults; a projection failure should not stop navigation or media Single place to enforce priority and avoid overlapping audio Well-defined, versionable, permission-checked inter-process interfaces Typed properties give apps safe, uniform access to vehicle data)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [30]
